{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-222568-r4513517","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Irish Pastie","sourcePageId":222568,"sourceRevision":"4513517","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:05:51Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Irish%20Pastie&oldid=4513517","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:00.536Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Northern Irish recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"ebec38b8eb398fd7a92d998bced994350b3e84860e8fbafdfe257f096527f91c","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Irish recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nNot to be confused with its Cornish counterpart, the '''pastie''' could be considered one of Northern Ireland's national dishes at it is regularly bought from chip shops across the province and generally can't be found anywhere else. Here is a recipe to try your own version.\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] ground [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] or [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]], cooked and drained\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]]\n* 1 medium-sized [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] and [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sautéed]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* ½ cup cold water\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* ½ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 3 medium-sized [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], boiled, mashed, and cooled\n* Fish batter\n\n==Procedure==\n# Combine the cooked meat, breadcrumbs, cooked onion, parsley, salt, pepper, Worcestershire sauce, water, coriander, and mashed potatoes.\n# Form the mixture into a disc about 3 [[Cookbook:Inch|inches]] in diameter.\n# Dip the disc into the batter so it's completely covered.\n# [[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Deep-fry]] in 375°F oil, and remove when golden brown.\n# Serve hot with chips (French fries).\n\n[[Category:Northern Irish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Irish Pastie","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 lb ground pork or beef, cooked and drained","sourceText":"1 lb ground pork or beef, cooked and drained","amountText":"1 lb ground pork or beef, cooked and drained","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup breadcrumbs","sourceText":"1 cup breadcrumbs","amountText":"1 cup breadcrumbs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 medium-sized onion, diced and sautéed","sourceText":"1 medium-sized onion, diced and sautéed","amountText":"1 medium-sized onion, diced and sautéed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tbsp chopped parsley","sourceText":"1 tbsp chopped parsley","amountText":"1 